    "--agent",
    "build",
    "--format",
    "json",
    "Complete this repository task: A `--no-x` flag is a negated option: it turns off `x`, so its parsed value must be stored under\nthe positive attribute name. Today `--no-color` is stored as `noColor` instead of `color`.\n\nFix `lib/option.js` so that a negated option's attribute name drops the `no-` prefix before\ncamelcasing, so `--no-color` becomes `color` and `--no-check-updates` becomes `checkUpdates`,\nwhile positive options are unaffected and a long flag that merely begins with the letters 'no'\n-- such as `--nozzle` -- is not treated as negated.\n\nParsing must then behave correctly: with only `--no-color` declared, the default is\n`{ color: true }` and passing the flag yields `{ color: false }`; when `--color` and `--no-color`\nare both declared they share the single `color` attribute and neither implies a default.\nWork only in the current repository. Do not push, open a PR, deploy, or access secrets.\nMake the smallest correct change and run relevant local checks."
  ],
